===============================================================================
HOW TO USE YOUR LEGAL COPY WITH THIS PROJECT
===============================================================================

1. Get the game from the source above and install it, or have your original
   disc ready.

2. Build the app (see README.md): run tools/package_app.sh, then open
   build/EpicPinballHD.app.

3. On first launch the app shows an import screen. Choose ONE of these:

   a. Original CD: the mounted disc, or a disc image you made of your own
      disc (.iso, .bin or .img).
   b. Installed DOS copy: the folder that contains EP1.EXE, SFX1.PIN,
      SONG1.PSM and so on (for example a copy of C:\EPIC).
   c. GOG, macOS version: install it with GOG Galaxy or the offline macOS
      installer, then choose the installed game (its .app or folder). The
      importer searches up to 6 folder levels deep, including inside .app
      bundles and .gog/.iso disc images.
   d. GOG, Windows installer on a Mac: unpack it first, for example with
      "brew install innoextract" and then
      "innoextract setup_epic_pinball_*.exe -d EpicPinballGOG", and choose
      the EpicPinballGOG folder.

   From the command line instead:
       EpicPinball --headless-import /path/to/your/copy

4. The import takes a few seconds. It only reads your copy and never changes
   it. The imported data is written to
   ~/Library/Application Support/EpicPinballHD/. To remove it, delete that
   folder.

The GOG edition has not been tested directly by this project. If the import
reports "no Epic Pinball table files", please open an issue that describes
your folder layout (file names only). Never attach or upload game files.

